<section class="contact-section">
	<h2>PhD and honours opportunities</h2>
	<p>
		We supervise students across the group's research themes. Projects
		usually sit somewhere between language technology and a real industrial
		problem, and many are run with an industry partner, so there is real data
		behind them.
	</p>
	<p>We are looking for students interested in any of the following:</p>
	<ul class="chevron-bullets extra-indent">
		<li>Entity recognition and lexical normalisation</li>
		<li>Knowledge graph construction from technical text</li>
		<li>Ontologies, knowledge representation and reasoning</li>
		<li>Annotation methods and annotation tooling</li>
		<li>Language models for specialist domains</li>
		<li>Adaptive user interfaces</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Before writing, have a look at <a href="/research/">what we work on</a> and
		mention which theme interests you and why. Send a CV, your transcript and
		a short note to
		<span class="crypted-email" data-name="wei.liu" data-domain="uwa" data-tld="edu.au"></span>.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you are not yet at UWA, you will also need to apply to a UWA program in
		Computer Science; the
		<a href="https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/courses/doctor-of-philosophy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">university's admission pages</a>
		cover entry requirements and scholarships.
	</p>
</section>
